{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums","id":928307,"title":"Homebrew Consiliums","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T11:44:58-07:00","id":928307,"title":"Homebrew Consiliums","content":"For all the Consilium examples forumites come up with.<br /> <hr /><br /> I don't actually have my own 2E one yet, other than a question: baring the terrible toll to Wisdom, how feasible would it be for a Consilium to require members to create a number of Soul Stones to limit their power, and help the Consilium? As mages prove themselves capable, they are allowed to &quot;reclaim&quot; their Soul Stones (and thus, advance their Gnosis). A wealth of Soul Stones in the mean time would greatly help with Demesne construction and potent magical tools for new members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:47:43-07:00","id":928309,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a pretty dictatorial Consilieum, but totally doable. Anyway, it doesn't risk the wisdom of the Councilor's themselves so what do they care if a few go Mad trying to pay the rent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:39:34-07:00","id":928349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums?p=928309#post928309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a pretty dictatorial Consilieum, but totally doable. Anyway, it doesn't risk the wisdom of the Councilor's themselves so what do they care if a few go Mad trying to pay the rent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;terrible toll on wisdom&quot; means statistically such an area would have higher than average abyssal intrusions due to paradox, all other factors being the same. Also as stated in the quote requiring a piece of your soul which can cast sympathetic magic upon you is an insanely high price for membership that almost no one would go into without threat of force unless they were completely ignorant about the potential consequences or already insane. A piece of you which allows attacks on the actual you is being held hostage in a very meaningful sense in your hypothetical scenario. It'd be like requiring citizens to wear remote controlled explosive collars.<br /> <br /> That being said, sounds like it fits the themes of enslavement in the Seers of the Throne nicely, and if you are thinking a group of mages are that focused on pragmatic mystical power generation at the cost of individual liberty, you're thinking of seers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-08-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:03:20-07:00","id":928364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums?p=928349#post928349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;terrible toll on wisdom&quot; means statistically such an area would have higher than average abyssal intrusions due to paradox, all other factors being the same. Also as stated in the quote requiring a piece of your soul which can cast sympathetic magic upon you is an insanely high price for membership that almost no one would go into without threat of force unless they were completely ignorant about the potential consequences or already insane. A piece of you which allows attacks on the actual you is being held hostage in a very meaningful sense in your hypothetical scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it also means you can detect a fair portion of stuff going on (Mage Sight detection through Soul Stones), that a good portion of the area will be a Demense, and &quot;they&quot; can always cast beneficial spells on you from afar, right? There's no way they'd use it solely to control and/or spy on you...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums?p=928349#post928349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be like requiring citizens to wear remote controlled explosive collars.</div> </div> </div> </div>And...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums?p=928349#post928349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, sounds like it fits the themes of enslavement in the Seers of the Throne nicely, and if you are thinking a group of mages are that focused on pragmatic mystical power generation at the cost of individual liberty, you're thinking of seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seer dominated &quot;Consilium&quot;, got it. I think I can work with that...<br /> <hr /><br /> Is there any way to mitigate or eliminate the Wisdom costs? Mind spells? Dread bargains?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:11:58-07:00","id":928373,"title":"","content":"Soul magic apparently can temporarily reduce your Wisdom, at least according to the Wisdom section of the book. Make your Wisdom lower than Soul Stone creation sin threshold, then cancel the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:31:06-07:00","id":928386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850762-101-bigass-mysteries\">This thread has some ideas for Consiliums.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:38:47-07:00","id":928390,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> considering the proliferation of Demesnes the likelihood of Paradaox or Abyssal incursion doesn't seem to me to actually be any higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:49:01-07:00","id":928452,"title":"","content":"This is a cool hook, it reminds me of the Tremere from Ars Magica where masters hold a mystical piece of their apprentice until they're strong enough to earn it back. And yeah, between the mention of Wisdom-reducing spells and the Masque merit letting you ignore certain Wisdom sins, you could totally justify not losing (as much?) Wisdom from making the soul stones. That would be a cool central Mystery for the setting, whatever weird Artifact or spell (or horrible imprisoned Lower Depths entity???) the Consilium subjects people to for temporarily suppressing Wisdom.<br /> <br /> It sounds like the kind of practice that some very old Consilium would have had on the books for centuries, and most people just don't really question it. It's a pain, but hey, it's tradition! I'm imagining some idyllic little hamlet in the Alps or somewhere picturesque, plenty of Hallows and Demesnes and a friendly Shadow and no Seers or Banishers around for miles, beautiful place- it's just that there's this one little catch if you want to stay.<br /> <br /> And this is exactly the kind of restrictive Diamond practice that the Nameless War was all about. What if the Free Council was never recognized as legitimate by this Consilium? I'm picturing something like The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas or maybe The Prisoner, where you introduce the PCs to this fascinating little world that doesn't extend any further than the borders of the hamlet, it seems lovely albeit a little strange, and slowly suggest that there are other mages Outside who have refused to give up their soulstones. Are they vicious Scelesti and Reapers who hate order and prey on mages foolish enough to leave the hamlet, or is it the Free Council building a community and safe haven for radicals, or something even stranger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 07-08-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:15:31-07:00","id":928490,"title":"","content":"After some thinking, I've arrived at a conclusion that any kind of Soul Magic that decreases your Wisdom would work in similar matter to Stealing The Fire; subject is immune to the Wisdom Degeneration, but they are merely postponed, and come all crashing down when you lift the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T02:38:00-07:00","id":928658,"title":"","content":"Still, this Consilium idea has a pretty fatal flaw - in order to create enough Soul Stones to actually hinder your Gnosis in any realistic term, you need to create about 8 or 9 of them. Wisdom risking is a secondary thing here (it's only an Understanding Wisdom sin, so you will stop rolling for this after a certain point, and with Willpower spending you have a decent chance of not losing it anyway); the primary thing here is the fact that each Soulstone costs it's creator a permanent Willpower dot.<br /> Your typical, Willpower-5 Mage will be only able to create 4 Soul Stones, which will limit them to Gnosis 6, which...isn't limiting, for most of the characters.<br /> Willpower 1, on the other hand, is a major problem. It's physically impossible to create enough Soul Stones to make you unable to progress your abilities without starting with something like Willpower 10.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-09-2016, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:38:33-07:00","id":928764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928307-homebrew-consiliums?p=928658#post928658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, this Consilium idea has a pretty fatal flaw - in order to create enough Soul Stones to actually hinder your Gnosis in any realistic term, you need to create about 8 or 9 of them. Wisdom risking is a secondary thing here (it's only an Understanding Wisdom sin, so you will stop rolling for this after a certain point, and with Willpower spending you have a decent chance of not losing it anyway); the primary thing here is the fact that each Soulstone costs it's creator a permanent Willpower dot.<br /> Your typical, Willpower-5 Mage will be only able to create 4 Soul Stones, which will limit them to Gnosis 6, which...isn't limiting, for most of the characters.<br /> Willpower 1, on the other hand, is a major problem. It's physically impossible to create enough Soul Stones to make you unable to progress your abilities without starting with something like Willpower 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't you buy Willpower dots back with Experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:42:27-07:00","id":928766,"title":"","content":"You can, but that's still a cost of 9 Experience to make enough Soul Stones so your New-On-The-Block Mage actually can't progress with his Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:01:18-07:00","id":928783,"title":"","content":"Easy enough to just say that PCs start the game with it, just like they don't have to spend Experiences on Order Status 1 or High Speech. It means that it's possible for characters to go rogue but that just adds potential plot threads!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:22:21-07:00","id":928798,"title":"","content":"If I were building that Consilium I'd probably only tax 7 soul stones, you still want members to be able to join legacies or they really will fuck off and letting them have that one potential Gnosis just beyond legacy entry makes you seem slightly nicer by opening up some of the more basic abilities Mages get access to as they increase Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T12:15:35-07:00","id":928858,"title":"","content":"Instead of assuming that people buy it back, I would probably create a Mystery based around it. For example, maybe there is a highly unstable Prelate of the Unity, who is literally taking the Willpower hits for the people, and gets his Dots back from their Exarch; imagine a Seer who sincerely follows this Mystery Command, hoping that their sacrifice will set the plan of Unity in motion.<br /> Or maybe instead of sacrificing their own WP instead of the WP of the taxed, it goes like that:<br /> <br /> Tax Payer pays their Willpower dot.<br /> Prelate transplants their own Willpower dot(s) to make up for whatever was lost.<br /> Prelate gets a refund from their Exarch.<br /> <br /> Repeat.<br /> <br /> This would mean that people are running around with their minds patched by Exarch-bestowed willpower. Sounds like a elaborate Chain setup...<br /> I really like this idea, not necessarily for this Consilium setup, but as a &quot;Here is this random Mage who can heal any kind of mind damage you can imagine, and they do it free of charge...better steer off unless you really need it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:46:34-07:00","id":956461,"title":"","content":"Since the last one went over so well, here's another partially formed idea: <hr /><br /> The Consilium is based in a small city or large town (large enough to have a noticeable population, but not enough to tip the boat). It is ruled by Spirit Mages who've &quot;domesticated&quot; the local Shadow and made themselves central to the local Spirit Courts. Their communal Sanctum is in the Shadow, they have Spirit servants who manage the city's domestic affairs in their favor (mostly just Influencing public servants, but occasionally Urging or even Possessing them, if needed), Spirit Familiars abound, and any other Spirits in the vicinity are required respect and heed Mages (even if they haven't &quot;earned&quot; it yet via Spirit 4's Attainment granting Honorary Rank). Status is pretty much based on a Mage's mastery of Spirit (leading to more Thyrsus, fewer Moros, at least in leadership positions).<br /> <br /> So, thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:44:44-07:00","id":956821,"title":"","content":"Instead of having the Mages 'domesticate' the local Shadow have there be one really powerful, dominant spirit in the area that the Mages have a working relationship with, a secret relationship that could go sour.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}